# Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension, or copy into Postman / Thunder Client.
@base = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Register -> 201
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "student@charusat.edu.in", "password": "secret123" }

### 2. Login -> 200 { token }
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "student@charusat.edu.in", "password": "secret123" }

### The token from the login response (REST Client fills this in automatically)
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 3. Current user -> 200
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Protected route without a token -> 401
GET {{base}}/tasks

### 5. Protected route with the token -> 200
GET {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Create a task -> 201
POST {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Protected task", "priority": "high" }

### 7. Malformed body (missing title) -> 400 before reaching MongoDB
POST {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "no title here" }

### 8. Tampered token -> 401
GET {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}x

### 9. Send this 3 times: first X-Cache: MISS, then HIT (compare the response times)
GET {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Single task, cached separately under its own key
GET {{base}}/tasks/<paste-an-_id-here>
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Cache hit/miss counters
GET {{base}}/debug/cache

### 12. Event-driven notification: response returns at once, watch the server console
POST {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Send weekly report" }

### 13. Triggers the 'error' listener (title contains fail-notify) — API still returns 201
POST {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "fail-notify demo" }
